{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-03T20:02:26.463Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"6da2f5f4d31f8f762cde8c96","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.316","source":"probe"}},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/body","value":"The CodeRabbit full review of PR 1654 (10:24Z, head 9e5407474) left four Minor findings. They were deferred under the bot-loop convergence rule so the PR could merge on green CI. Each one was checked against the code.\n1. docs/CONFIGURATION.md: the governance.start_blocker_enforcement row lists only update --status in_progress and claim --start. It omits claim --next --start and start-task, which take the same admission check.\n2. sdk/public-surface.json: ItemRevisionConflictRowFields is not an exported snapshot symbol, so the snapshot cannot detect changes to the inherited conflict fields on bulk and history rows.\n3. src/sdk/lifecycle/claim.ts: in the claim --next candidate loop, any error other than already_claimed_by is rethrown. A candidate whose blocker opens between ranking and the locked start therefore ends the pass, and later healthy candidates are not attempted. The refused candidate is not written.\n4. src/sdk/lifecycle/close.ts: the post-close dependent revision conflict spreads the dependent conflict's required/nextSteps text. That text tells the caller to retry the close with --expect-hash, but the close has already committed, and a repeat close is refused as terminal without --force."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-mrvq8u"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"Start-blocker and revision-conflict follow-ups from the PR 1654 CodeRabbit full review"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":""},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":3},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["docs","expected-revision","pm-gh1576","pm-urzubi","start-blockers"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-11-03T20:02:26.463Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-03T20:02:26.463Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:claude-code"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":120},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"The CONFIGURATION.md row names all four start paths (update --status in_progress, claim --start, claim --next --start, start-task); ItemRevisionConflictRowFields is exported and the regenerated SDK surface snapshot records its fields; claim --next --start skips a candidate refused with start_blocked_by_open_dependency and claims the next eligible candidate, with a spec; the post-close dependent_revision_conflict refusal says the close is complete and names only the dependent unblock as the remaining step, with a spec"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-doxj"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"low"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/severity","value":"low"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-gh1576","kind":"discovered_from","created_at":"2026-11-03T20:02:26.463Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-urzubi","kind":"discovered_from","created_at":"2026-11-03T20:02:26.463Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"}]}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"ea4a91d16cb00c672c4b1964d173c2229828b8c49f9e61ecdab88daa793d052c","item_hash_version":3,"message":"","context":{"agent_proven