{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-04T10:03:52.722Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"436e44ca2d204a1ee603915a","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.317","source":"probe"}},"op":"update","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/resolution","value":"docs/CONFIGURATION.md and docs/COMMANDS.md name all four start paths and the skip; ItemRevisionConflictRowFields is exported and snapshotted; claimNextFromRecommendations skips a candidate refused with start_blocked_by_open_dependency (refused inside the claim's locked mutation, so nothing is written) and reports start_refused on the result, in compact output and in the exhausted refusal's details. The post-close dependent revision conflict says the close is complete and separates two groups: guarded dependents refused for a revision conflict are listed in details.pending_unblock, each with a get step and an unblock step in the caller's tracker scope using the configured open status; dependents whose unblock failed for another reason are listed with their reasons in details.auto_unblock_failed, get only, and must have that cause fixed first. The report is fitted under the error-details ceiling with *_omitted counts, and adds a paged discovery step across every blocked-role status whenever ids or steps were cut."},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-04T10:03:52.722Z"}],"before_hash":"919704275959ab46c57fdb9ac2bc4f38fc2ceb3660a8f625a29a781ab4efc9b0","after_hash":"6011a7a2fc3ee2db6a70e051fc158d6da63c5c843ed3a41ea75a425f5586aa59","item_hash_version":3,"message":"Distinguish revision conflicts from other failed unblocks in the resolution (CodeRabbit PR 1658)","context":{"agent_provenance_outcom